<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khuman Singh of Charkhari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khuman Singh was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundela</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhatrasal">Maharaja Chhatrasal</a> through the Jaitpur branch, who founded the state of Charkhari in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> around 1765 on his share of the family lands. His successors were confirmed by the British in 1804, and the state remained a princely state until it was merged into Vindhya Pradesh after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a>.</p></div>
